# Interactions (Tab, drop settle + flash, inspector-edit flash):
#   BOWSHOCK_FREEZE_FLASH=1 cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/interactions.drive out/interactions
#   BOWSHOCK_DRIVE_TAB=1 cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/interactions.drive out/interactions-tab
# BOWSHOCK_FREEZE_FLASH holds a flash at its first frame (a headless run delivers no frame ticks), so the screenshot right
# after a drop or a committed edit shows the accent outline, the lifted part and the flashing lane bar. A headless run also
# delivers no key subscription events, so BOWSHOCK_DRIVE_TAB=1 presses Tab once at start-up (the key itself is unit-tested).
viewport 1280x800
screenshot 1-start.png

# Drag a body tube out of the parts bin onto the rocket: attach nodes show, the ghost follows the nearest one.
press "Body tube"
move (200, 200)
move (400, 300)
move (600, 330)
screenshot 2-drag.png
release (600, 330)
screenshot 3-dropped-flash.png
# A committed inspector edit flashes the part it changed: pick the booster's lane bar, type a new length in the Inspector.
click (872, 596)
click (1175, 133)
type "300"
type enter
screenshot 4-edit-flash.png
